## Feature 1: ZIP Upload Support

### Install JSZip
Run: `npm install jszip` (or add it — check if it's already in package.json)

### Modify `src/components/BulkUploadZone.tsx`

Currently accepts individual files (PDF, DOCX, etc). Add ZIP support:

1. Add `.zip` to accepted file extensions and MIME types (`application/zip`, `application/x-zip-compressed`)
2. When a .zip file is dropped/selected:
   - Import JSZip dynamically: `const JSZip = (await import('jszip')).default;`
   - Read the ZIP: `const zip = await JSZip.loadAsync(file);`
   - Extract all files from the ZIP
   - Filter: only keep files with allowed resume extensions (PDF, DOCX, DOC, RTF, TXT)
   - Add extracted files to the upload queue (same as individual files)
   - Show toast: "Extracted X resumes from ZIP file"
   - Skip non-resume files silently (images, folders, etc.)

3. Update the drop zone text: "Drop resumes or ZIP files here"
4. Update accepted file info: "PDF, DOCX, DOC, RTF, TXT, or ZIP"

The extraction should happen BEFORE files enter the queue. The existing per-file upload logic handles the rest.

Key implementation in handleFileDrop/handleFileSelect:
```typescript
const processFiles = async (rawFiles: File[]) => {
  const resumeFiles: File[] = [];

  for (const file of rawFiles) {
    if (file.name.toLowerCase().endsWith('.zip')) {
      try {
        const JSZip = (await import('jszip')).default;
        const zip = await JSZip.loadAsync(file);
        for (const [path, zipEntry] of Object.entries(zip.files)) {
          if (zipEntry.dir) continue;
          const ext = path.split('.').pop()?.toLowerCase();
          if (!['pdf', 'docx', 'doc', 'rtf', 'txt'].includes(ext || '')) continue;
          const blob = await zipEntry.async('blob');
          const extractedFile = new File([blob], zipEntry.name.split('/').pop() || path, {
            type: getMimeType(ext || ''),
          });
          resumeFiles.push(extractedFile);
        }
        toast.success(`Extracted ${resumeFiles.length} resumes from ${file.name}`);
      } catch {
        toast.error(`Failed to extract ${file.name}`);
      }
    } else {
      resumeFiles.push(file);
    }
  }

  return resumeFiles;
};
```

Helper for MIME type:
```typescript
function getMimeType(ext: string): string {
  const map: Record<string, string> = {
    pdf: 'application/pdf',
    docx: 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document',
    doc: 'application/msword',
    rtf: 'application/rtf',
    txt: 'text/plain',
  };
  return map[ext] || 'application/octet-stream';
}
```

